4.1.evidence:
Article 17
(1) Prevention of violence against women and children is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by regional apparatus that has the main duties and functions of coordination in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:
a. establishing a working network in efforts to prevent violence;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. providing counseling/guidance;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
e. providing critical education about the rights of women and children for the community.

